///$tab Main
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Main
   Purpose: entry point, house regional settings, data model
            documentation, Desktop conversion notes
   Inputs:  none                Outputs: none
   =====================================================

   APP: Sales Demo (Qlik Sense Desktop edition)

   PURPOSE
     Showcase / demo app for a typical sales analytics use case
     (orders, customers, products, calendar). Built to demonstrate a
     proper star-schema model and house scripting conventions when no
     real data source is available.

   PROVENANCE — this is a CONVERTED script
     Converted from the Qlik Cloud original at
       scripts/sales-demo/sales-demo.qvs
     which remains the canonical Cloud version and is unmodified.
     Three classes of change were made; all are marked in-line with
     the tag  // DESKTOP:  or  // FIX F1:  so they can be found with a
     single search.

       1. QVD paths repointed from a Cloud space connection to a local
          Desktop folder connection. See the DESKTOP PORTING CONTRACT
          in the Variables tab — the conversion is TWO LINES.
       2. FIX F1 (Critical, INHERITED from the Cloud original — it was
          present there and is not introduced by this conversion):
          FACT_Sales and DIM_Product both carried [Unit Cost (USD)] as
          well as %ProductKey, which is two shared field names between
          two tables and therefore a $Syn table at the Data Model
          layer. The fact-side lookup is now resolved into a working
          field _UnitCostResolved, consumed to derive
          [Cost Amount (USD)], and DROP FIELDed before the STORE so it
          never reaches Transform_FACT_Sales.qvd or the model.
          [Unit Cost (USD)] is now canonical on DIM_Product alone.
       3. Two minor house-convention fixes: vL.ScriptVersion moved from
          this tab to the Variables tab where all variables belong, and
          vL.Today (previously declared and never referenced) is now
          used consistently for every "as at today" calculation.

   DATA SOURCES
     None — all data is generated synthetically inline in the Extract
     tab using AUTOGENERATE / RAND() / RecNo() / Pick(). There is no
     external connection, database or file behind this app. The script
     still follows the normal 3-tier QVD layering (Extract / Transform
     / Data Model) so the pattern matches a production script exactly.

   RELOAD CADENCE
     On demand only. Qlik Sense Desktop has no reload scheduler and no
     reload tasks, so every reload here is manual (hub "Load data", or
     the engine reload API). Each reload regenerates a fresh random
     dataset (RAND() is not seeded) — row counts stay constant but
     values differ reload to reload. Expected and acceptable for a demo.

   SECTION ACCESS
     Deliberately not implemented, exactly as in the Cloud original. No
     row-level security was requested for this demo app. Note that Qlik
     Sense Desktop does not authenticate users at all, so a Section
     Access block could not be validated on this machine even if one
     existed — a clean Desktop reload would prove nothing about it. If
     row-level security ever becomes a requirement, add the tab before
     Exit following the house pattern (Star is *, UPPER() matching,
     non-author ADMIN row) and validate it on Qlik Cloud or QSEoW on a
     clone before trusting it.

   OWNER
     Shaun Somai (script author / requester)

   VERSION
     See vL.ScriptVersion in the Variables tab. Bump semantically on
     structural changes to the model or script.

   DATA MODEL DIAGRAM (star schema, one fact)

       DIM_Date                     DIM_Customer
       (Order Date)                 (%CustomerKey)
            \                             |
             \                            |
              \                           v
               +---------------->  FACT_Sales  <----------------+
                                  (%OrderLineKey)                |
                                  grain: 1 row per order line     |
                                                                   \
                                                              DIM_Product
                                                              (%ProductKey)

     - DIM_Date associates to FACT_Sales purely by the shared field
       name [Order Date] — no synthetic key. [Ship Date] is kept on
       FACT_Sales as an unlinked attribute field (one canonical date
       per fact); it is NOT aliased into the calendar.
     - DIM_Customer / DIM_Product associate via single-field surrogate
       keys %CustomerKey / %ProductKey. After FIX F1, %ProductKey is
       the ONLY field name shared between FACT_Sales and DIM_Product.
     - Single fact table, classic star: no concatenation or link table
       was needed.
   ===================================================== */

// House regional settings.
// UNSURE — verify: no CLAUDE.md exists in this project, so no house
// regional convention could be read from it. These values are carried
// over verbatim from the Cloud original; none of them require a change
// on Qlik Sense Desktop. Confirm they are correct for the org and
// record them in CLAUDE.md so future scripts stay consistent.
SET HidePrefix='_';
SET ThousandSep=',';
SET DecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyThousandSep=',';
SET MoneyDecimalSep='.';
SET MoneyFormat='$#,##0.00;-$#,##0.00';
SET TimeFormat='hh:mm:ss';
SET DateFormat='YYYY-MM-DD';
SET TimestampFormat='YYYY-MM-DD hh:mm:ss[.fff]';
SET FirstWeekDay=0;
SET BrokenWeeks=0;
SET ReferenceDay=4;
SET FirstMonthOfYear=1;
SET CollationLocale='en-GB';
SET CreateSearchIndexOnReload=1;
SET MonthNames='Jan;Feb;Mar;Apr;May;Jun;Jul;Aug;Sep;Oct;Nov;Dec';
SET LongMonthNames='January;February;March;April;May;June;July;August;September;October;November;December';
SET DayNames='Mon;Tue;Wed;Thu;Fri;Sat;Sun';
SET LongDayNames='Monday;Tuesday;Wednesday;Thursday;Friday;Saturday;Sunday';
SET NumericalAbbreviation='3:k;6:M;9:G;12:T;15:P;18:E;21:Z;24:Y;-3:m;-6:μ;-9:n;-12:p;-15:f;-18:a;-21:z;-24:y';

// No Section Access tab in this script, so "Star is *;" is not required.
// DESKTOP: vL.ScriptVersion was declared here in the Cloud original.
// It has been moved to the Variables tab where every variable belongs.


///$tab Variables
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Variables
   Purpose: all script variables, declared once, prefixed vL./vG./vD./vP./vT.
            No variable is ever declared inline elsewhere in the script.
   Inputs:  none                Outputs: none
   ===================================================== */

// ---- vL. run-control values ----
// DESKTOP: moved here from the Main tab (house rule: variables are
// declared in the Variables tab only).
LET vL.ScriptVersion    = '1.1.0-desktop';

// DESKTOP: vL.Today was declared but never referenced in the Cloud
// original. It is now the single "as at" date for the whole reload and
// is used everywhere Today() previously appeared inline, so one long
// reload cannot straddle midnight and silently use two different days.
// Num() is essential: LET stores the EVALUATED result, so a bare
// Today() would store the formatted string '2026-09-15', and the
// expansion $(vL.Today) would then be parsed as the arithmetic
// 2026 - 09 - 15 = 2002. Num() stores the date serial instead.
LET vL.Today            = Num(Today());

LET vL.ScriptStartTime  = Now();
LET vL.RowsCustomers    = 200;    // DIM_Customer target row count
LET vL.RowsProducts     = 150;    // DIM_Product target row count
LET vL.RowsOrderLines   = 6000;   // FACT_Sales target row count (grain: 1 row = 1 order line)
// Orders header count. ~2.5 lines per order, so this must stay in step with
// the Ceil(RecNo()/2.5) grouping in the Extract tab: every generated line
// looks its order attributes up by OrderID, and an order with no header row
// would fall through to the ApplyMap defaults.
LET vL.RowsOrders       = Ceil($(vL.RowsOrderLines)/2.5);  // = 2400 order headers

// ---- vL. working counters — declared here, assigned where used ----
// Placeholders so that no variable is first created inline elsewhere.
// vL.RowCount is assigned inside SUB storeAndDrop; the *Count/*Distinct
// pairs are assigned by the key-uniqueness checks in the Transform tab.
LET vL.RowCount      = 0;
LET vL.CustCount     = 0;
LET vL.CustDistinct  = 0;
LET vL.ProdCount     = 0;
LET vL.ProdDistinct  = 0;
LET vL.FactCount     = 0;
LET vL.FactDistinct  = 0;
LET vL.DateCount     = 0;
LET vL.DateDistinct  = 0;

// ---- vD. dates ----
LET vD.Format       = 'YYYY-MM-DD';   // matches Main's SET DateFormat above
LET vD.MinDate      = 0;   // placeholder — overwritten in Transform from FACT_Sales' [Order Date] range (date serial)
LET vD.MaxDate      = 0;   // placeholder — overwritten in Transform from FACT_Sales' [Order Date] range (date serial)
LET vD.MinDateLabel = '';  // placeholder — human-readable form of vD.MinDate, for the calendar TRACE only
LET vD.MaxDateLabel = '';  // placeholder — human-readable form of vD.MaxDate, for the calendar TRACE only

/* ---- vP. QVD paths ------------------------------------------------
   DESKTOP PORTING CONTRACT — READ THIS BEFORE THE FIRST RELOAD

   These two LET statements are the ONLY environment-specific lines in
   the entire script. Everything downstream addresses QVDs through
   $(vP.QVD_Extract) and $(vP.QVD_Transform), so moving this app
   between Qlik Sense Desktop and Qlik Cloud is a two-line edit and
   nothing else.

   CURRENT SETTING — Qlik Sense Desktop (this machine)
     Reads and writes through a local FOLDER data connection named
     DEMO_QVDS_LOCAL, which must be created inside this app (Desktop
     stores data connections per-app, inside the .qvf) and pointed at:

         C:\Qlik\Sense\QVD\SalesDemo

     Two subfolders must exist on disk before the first reload, because
     Qlik's STORE statement writes files but never creates directories:

         C:\Qlik\Sense\QVD\SalesDemo\Extract
         C:\Qlik\Sense\QVD\SalesDemo\Transform

     A lib:// folder connection is used rather than a bare absolute
     path deliberately: absolute paths only work while Desktop is in
     legacy reload mode (StandardReload=0), which is the default but is
     a machine-level setting outside this script's control, whereas a
     folder connection reloads correctly under either mode.

   TO REVERSE THE CONVERSION — port this script back to Qlik Cloud
     Edit the two LET statements immediately below, and nothing else in
     the script, restoring the Cloud original's values:

         vP.QVD_Extract    ->  lib://DEMO_QVDS/Extract/
         vP.QVD_Transform  ->  lib://DEMO_QVDS/Transform/

     DEMO_QVDS is the Cloud-side space connection name. UNSURE —
     verify: it was a placeholder in the Cloud original too and must
     exist in the target space before that script can reload there.

     Alternatively, name the Desktop folder connection DEMO_QVDS rather
     than DEMO_QVDS_LOCAL and restore the two paths above permanently —
     the script is then byte-identical in both environments and the
     lib:// alias alone carries the difference. The distinct Desktop
     name is used here only so it is unambiguous, at a glance, which
     environment a given copy of the script is pointed at.
   ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
// DESKTOP: converted from 'lib://DEMO_QVDS/Extract/'   (see contract above)
LET vP.QVD_Extract   = 'lib://DEMO_QVDS_LOCAL/Extract/';
// DESKTOP: converted from 'lib://DEMO_QVDS/Transform/' (see contract above)
LET vP.QVD_Transform = 'lib://DEMO_QVDS_LOCAL/Transform/';

// ---- vG. reusable expressions (parenthesised so precedence can't
//         silently break when composed into a larger expression) ----
SET vG.GrossMargin = (Sum([Sales Amount (USD)]) - Sum([Cost Amount (USD)]));
SET vG.MarginPct   = (($(vG.GrossMargin)) / Sum([Sales Amount (USD)]));


///$tab Libraries
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Libraries
   Purpose: reusable subroutines, defined before use
   Inputs:  none                Outputs: none
   ===================================================== */

// storeAndDrop: STOREs a resident table to the given QVD path, TRACEs
// its row count, then DROPs it from memory. Used by every Extract and
// Transform output table so STORE always happens before DROP and every
// layer logs a row count without repeating the same three lines.
SUB storeAndDrop(iTableName, iQvdPath)
    LET vL.RowCount = NoOfRows('$(iTableName)');
    STORE [$(iTableName)] INTO [$(iQvdPath)];
    TRACE >>> $(iTableName): $(vL.RowCount) rows stored to $(iQvdPath);
    DROP TABLE [$(iTableName)];
END SUB


///$tab Extract
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Extract
   Purpose: generate synthetic "source" data (no external connection
            exists for this demo) and land one QVD per source table,
            raw and unmodified.
   Inputs:  none (AUTOGENERATE / RAND() / RecNo() / Pick())
   Outputs: Extract_Demo_Customers.qvd, Extract_Demo_Products.qvd,
            Extract_Demo_OrderLines.qvd
   Note:    the first STORE in this tab is the script's canary — if the
            DEMO_QVDS_LOCAL connection or the Extract folder is missing,
            the reload fails here with a legible path error rather than
            producing a half-built model.
   ===================================================== */

// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Extract_Demo_Customers
// Simulates a raw customer export: source-style column names, and a
// signup date deliberately carried as a DD/MM/YYYY text string (via
// Text()) so the Transform layer demonstrates explicit Date#() parsing
// rather than letting Qlik guess a format.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_Customers_Seed:
LOAD
    RecNo()                            AS CustomerID,
    Ceil(Rand()*8)                     AS _GeoIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*4)                     AS _SegIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*12)                    AS _FNameIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*12)                    AS _LNameIdx,
    Floor($(vL.Today) - Rand()*1460)   AS _SignupDateNum   // up to 4 years back
AUTOGENERATE $(vL.RowsCustomers);

Extract_Demo_Customers:
LOAD
    CustomerID,
    Pick(_FNameIdx,'James','Mary','Robert','Patricia','John','Jennifer','Michael','Linda','William','Elizabeth','David','Susan')
        & ' ' &
    Pick(_LNameIdx,'Smith','Johnson','Williams','Brown','Jones','Garcia','Miller','Davis','Rodriguez','Martinez','Hernandez','Lopez')
                                                             AS CUST_NM,
    Pick(_SegIdx,'Consumer','Corporate','Small Business','Enterprise')                    AS Segment,
    Pick(_GeoIdx,'United Kingdom','United States','United States','Germany','France','Australia','Canada','Spain') AS Country,
    Pick(_GeoIdx,'London','New York','Chicago','Berlin','Paris','Sydney','Toronto','Madrid')                       AS City,
    Pick(_GeoIdx,'EMEA','AMER','AMER','EMEA','EMEA','APAC','AMER','EMEA')                                          AS Region,
    Text(Date(_SignupDateNum,'DD/MM/YYYY'))                    AS SignupDateRaw
RESIDENT TMP_Customers_Seed;

DROP TABLE TMP_Customers_Seed;

CALL storeAndDrop('Extract_Demo_Customers', '$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_Customers.qvd');

// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Extract_Demo_Products
// Category and Sub Category are drawn together (nested Pick keyed off
// the same _CatIdx/_SubIdx draw) so the pairing stays realistic
// (e.g. Electronics never pairs with a Furniture sub-category).
// List price / unit cost carried as formatted Dual values to mirror a
// typical source export, then stripped of formatting in Transform.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_Products_Seed:
LOAD
    RecNo()                AS ProductID,
    Ceil(Rand()*5)          AS _CatIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*3)          AS _SubIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*4)          AS _BrandIdx,
    Ceil(Rand()*9000)       AS _NameSeq,
    5 + Rand()*495          AS _ListPrice
AUTOGENERATE $(vL.RowsProducts);

Extract_Demo_Products:
LOAD
    ProductID,
    Pick(_CatIdx,'Electronics','Office Supplies','Furniture','Apparel','Food & Beverage') AS Category,
    Pick(_CatIdx,
        Pick(_SubIdx,'Laptops','Smartphones','Accessories'),
        Pick(_SubIdx,'Paper & Stationery','Printers','Storage'),
        Pick(_SubIdx,'Desks','Chairs','Shelving'),
        Pick(_SubIdx,'Outerwear','Footwear','Accessories'),
        Pick(_SubIdx,'Snacks','Beverages','Bakery')
    )                                                                                     AS SubCategory,
    Pick(_BrandIdx,'Acme','Zenith','Nova','Orbit')                                        AS Brand,
    Pick(_BrandIdx,'Acme','Zenith','Nova','Orbit') & ' ' &
        Pick(_CatIdx,
            Pick(_SubIdx,'Laptop','Smartphone','Accessory'),
            Pick(_SubIdx,'Stationery Set','Printer','Storage Unit'),
            Pick(_SubIdx,'Desk','Chair','Shelving Unit'),
            Pick(_SubIdx,'Jacket','Shoe','Bag'),
            Pick(_SubIdx,'Snack Pack','Beverage Case','Bakery Box')
        ) & ' ' & _NameSeq                                                                AS PROD_NM,
    Num(_ListPrice,'#,##0.00')                                                            AS ListPriceRaw,
    Num(_ListPrice * (0.4 + Rand()*0.3),'#,##0.00')                                       AS UnitCostRaw
RESIDENT TMP_Products_Seed;

DROP TABLE TMP_Products_Seed;

CALL storeAndDrop('Extract_Demo_Products', '$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_Products.qvd');

// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Extract_Demo_Orders  (header, not exported)
// Grain: one row per order.
//
// FIX: an order's customer, date, channel and rep are properties of the
// ORDER, not of each line. Generating them per line with Rand() gave every
// OrderID 2-3 different customers and 2-3 different dates, which made
// Count(DISTINCT [Order ID]), Average Order Value and any YTD order count
// meaningless. Generate the header first, then have the lines inherit from
// it by OrderID.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_Orders_Seed:
LOAD
    RecNo()                                             AS OrderID,
    Ceil(Rand()*$(vL.RowsCustomers))                    AS CustomerID,
    Floor($(vL.Today) - Rand()*730)                     AS _OrderDateNum,   // up to 2 years back
    Ceil(Rand()*7)                                      AS _ShipLagDays,    // ships 1-7 days after order
    Pick(Ceil(Rand()*3),'Online','Retail','Partner')    AS SalesChannel,
    Pick(Ceil(Rand()*8),'A. Nguyen','B. Carter','C. Patel','D. Novak','E. Silva','F. Kowalski','G. Andersen','H. Okafor') AS SalesRep
AUTOGENERATE $(vL.RowsOrders);

// One mapping table per order-level attribute. Mapping tables are never
// dropped explicitly -- DROP TABLE cannot resolve them and aborts the reload;
// Qlik discards them itself at the end of the script.
MAP_OrderCustomer:
MAPPING LOAD OrderID, CustomerID     RESIDENT TMP_Orders_Seed;
MAP_OrderDate:
MAPPING LOAD OrderID, _OrderDateNum  RESIDENT TMP_Orders_Seed;
MAP_OrderShipLag:
MAPPING LOAD OrderID, _ShipLagDays   RESIDENT TMP_Orders_Seed;
MAP_OrderChannel:
MAPPING LOAD OrderID, SalesChannel   RESIDENT TMP_Orders_Seed;
MAP_OrderRep:
MAPPING LOAD OrderID, SalesRep       RESIDENT TMP_Orders_Seed;

DROP TABLE TMP_Orders_Seed;

// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// Extract_Demo_OrderLines
// Raw transactional export — the future FACT_Sales source. Grain: one
// row per order line. Product, quantity, price and discount vary by
// line; customer, date, ship lag, channel and rep are inherited from
// the order header so they are constant within an order. Dates carried
// as DD/MM/YYYY text, exactly like the customer extract, to force
// explicit Date#() parsing downstream.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_OrderLines_Seed:
LOAD
    *,
    ApplyMap('MAP_OrderCustomer', OrderID, 1)           AS CustomerID,
    ApplyMap('MAP_OrderDate',     OrderID, $(vL.Today)) AS _OrderDateNum,
    ApplyMap('MAP_OrderShipLag',  OrderID, 1)           AS _ShipLagDays,
    ApplyMap('MAP_OrderChannel',  OrderID, 'Online')    AS SalesChannel,
    ApplyMap('MAP_OrderRep',      OrderID, 'A. Nguyen') AS SalesRep;
LOAD
    RecNo()                                            AS OrderLineID,
    Ceil(RecNo()/2.5)                                  AS OrderID,
    Ceil(Rand()*$(vL.RowsProducts))                     AS ProductID,
    Ceil(Rand()*8)                                      AS Quantity,
    10 + Rand()*490                                     AS _UnitPrice,
    Pick(Ceil(Rand()*5),0,0,0.05,0.1,0.15)              AS DiscountPct      // most lines undiscounted
AUTOGENERATE $(vL.RowsOrderLines);

Extract_Demo_OrderLines:
LOAD
    OrderLineID,
    OrderID,
    CustomerID,
    ProductID,
    Text(Date(_OrderDateNum,'DD/MM/YYYY'))                 AS OrderDateRaw,
    Text(Date(_OrderDateNum + _ShipLagDays,'DD/MM/YYYY'))  AS ShipDateRaw,
    Quantity,
    Num(_UnitPrice,'#,##0.00')                              AS UnitPriceRaw,
    DiscountPct,
    SalesChannel,
    SalesRep
RESIDENT TMP_OrderLines_Seed;

DROP TABLE TMP_OrderLines_Seed;

CALL storeAndDrop('Extract_Demo_OrderLines', '$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_OrderLines.qvd');


///$tab Transform
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Transform
   Purpose: cleanse the extract layer, resolve business names, build
            keys, resolve the product-cost lookup, build the master
            calendar. Every load in this tab is deliberately
            non-optimised (this is the cleansing layer by design) —
            optimised loads only start at the Data Model layer.
   Inputs:  Extract_*.qvd       Outputs: Transform_FACT_Sales.qvd,
                                         Transform_DIM_Customer.qvd,
                                         Transform_DIM_Product.qvd,
                                         Transform_DIM_Date.qvd
   ===================================================== */

// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// DIM_Customer
// Grain: one row per customer (%CustomerKey unique)
// Source: Extract_Demo_Customers.qvd
// Notes: SignupDateRaw parsed from its source DD/MM/YYYY string with
//        Date#() then re-formatted to the house date format.
//        _NewCustomer is a pre-computed flag (signed up in the last
//        90 days) so the front end can use set analysis instead of
//        an If() inside an aggregation.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_Customers:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_Customers.qvd] (qvd);

DIM_Customer:
LOAD
    CustomerID                                                      AS %CustomerKey,
    Trim(CUST_NM)                                                   AS [Customer Name],
    Segment                                                         AS [Segment],
    Country                                                         AS [Country],
    City                                                            AS [City],
    Region                                                          AS [Region],
    Date(Date#(SignupDateRaw,'DD/MM/YYYY'),'$(vD.Format)')          AS [Signup Date],
    If($(vL.Today) - Date#(SignupDateRaw,'DD/MM/YYYY') <= 90, 1, 0) AS _NewCustomer
RESIDENT TMP_Customers;

DROP TABLE TMP_Customers;

TAG FIELD [Customer Name] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Segment] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Country] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [City] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Region] WITH '$dimension';

// Dimension key uniqueness check
TMP_CustomerKeyCheck:
LOAD
    Count(%CustomerKey)          AS RowCount,
    Count(DISTINCT %CustomerKey) AS DistinctCount
RESIDENT DIM_Customer;

LET vL.CustCount    = Peek('RowCount', 0, 'TMP_CustomerKeyCheck');
LET vL.CustDistinct = Peek('DistinctCount', 0, 'TMP_CustomerKeyCheck');
IF $(vL.CustCount) <> $(vL.CustDistinct) THEN
    TRACE >>> WARNING: DIM_Customer %CustomerKey is not unique ($(vL.CustCount) rows vs $(vL.CustDistinct) distinct);
ELSE
    TRACE >>> DIM_Customer %CustomerKey uniqueness OK ($(vL.CustDistinct) customers);
END IF
DROP TABLE TMP_CustomerKeyCheck;

CALL storeAndDrop('DIM_Customer', '$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Customer.qvd');


// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// DIM_Product
// Grain: one row per product (%ProductKey unique)
// Source: Extract_Demo_Products.qvd
// Notes: ListPriceRaw / UnitCostRaw arrive as formatted Dual values
//        (simulating a typical source export) and are stripped back
//        to plain numerics with Floor(x*100)/100 — formatting belongs
//        on the front-end master measure, not on the stored field.
//        FIX F1: DIM_Product is the SOLE owner of [Unit Cost (USD)].
//        FACT_Sales must never carry a field of that name — see the
//        FACT_Sales block below.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_Products:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_Products.qvd] (qvd);

DIM_Product:
LOAD
    ProductID                    AS %ProductKey,
    Trim(PROD_NM)                AS [Product Name],
    Category                     AS [Category],
    SubCategory                  AS [Sub Category],
    Brand                        AS [Brand],
    Floor(ListPriceRaw*100)/100  AS [List Price (USD)],
    Floor(UnitCostRaw*100)/100   AS [Unit Cost (USD)]
RESIDENT TMP_Products;

DROP TABLE TMP_Products;

TAG FIELD [Product Name] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Category] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Sub Category] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Brand] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [List Price (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Unit Cost (USD)] WITH '$measure';

// Dimension key uniqueness check
TMP_ProductKeyCheck:
LOAD
    Count(%ProductKey)          AS RowCount,
    Count(DISTINCT %ProductKey) AS DistinctCount
RESIDENT DIM_Product;

LET vL.ProdCount    = Peek('RowCount', 0, 'TMP_ProductKeyCheck');
LET vL.ProdDistinct = Peek('DistinctCount', 0, 'TMP_ProductKeyCheck');
IF $(vL.ProdCount) <> $(vL.ProdDistinct) THEN
    TRACE >>> WARNING: DIM_Product %ProductKey is not unique ($(vL.ProdCount) rows vs $(vL.ProdDistinct) distinct);
ELSE
    TRACE >>> DIM_Product %ProductKey uniqueness OK ($(vL.ProdDistinct) products);
END IF
DROP TABLE TMP_ProductKeyCheck;

// Single-field lookup used by FACT_Sales below to resolve transacted
// unit cost per line — built from DIM_Product while it is still
// resident, dropped again once FACT_Sales has consumed it.
MAP_ProductCost:
MAPPING LOAD
    %ProductKey,
    [Unit Cost (USD)]
RESIDENT DIM_Product;

CALL storeAndDrop('DIM_Product', '$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Product.qvd');


// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// FACT_Sales
// Grain: one row per order line
// Source: Extract_Demo_OrderLines.qvd
// Notes: Unit cost resolved via MAP_ProductCost (single-field lookup,
//        default 0 explained: an unmatched product would indicate a
//        broken extract, so 0 cost makes the gap visible in margin
//        rather than silently dropping the row). Gross Sales /
//        Discount Amount / Sales Amount / Cost Amount are all
//        pre-calculated here (three stacked preceding loads) so the
//        front end uses stored measures and set analysis rather than
//        If()/derived math inside chart expressions.
//
//        FIX F1 (Critical, inherited from the Cloud original): the
//        ApplyMap lookup previously landed as [Unit Cost (USD)], a
//        name DIM_Product also uses. Two tables sharing both
//        %ProductKey and [Unit Cost (USD)] is the textbook synthetic
//        key, and the outer preceding load's * carried the offending
//        field into Transform_FACT_Sales.qvd and on into the model.
//        The lookup now lands as the working field _UnitCostResolved,
//        is consumed to derive [Cost Amount (USD)], and is DROP
//        FIELDed below before the STORE — so it exists only inside
//        this tab, never in the QVD and never in the data model.
//        %ProductKey is now the only field shared with DIM_Product.
//        The [Unit Cost (USD)] $measure tag that sat in this block in
//        the Cloud original has been removed with it; DIM_Product
//        already tags the canonical field.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_OrderLines:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Extract)Extract_Demo_OrderLines.qvd] (qvd);

FACT_Sales:
LOAD
    *,
    Round([Quantity] * [_UnitCostResolved], 0.01) AS [Cost Amount (USD)];   // FIX F1: derived from the working field
LOAD
    *,
    Round([Quantity] * [Unit Price (USD)], 0.01)                        AS [Gross Sales (USD)],
    Round([Quantity] * [Unit Price (USD)] * [Discount Pct], 0.01)       AS [Discount Amount (USD)],
    Round([Quantity] * [Unit Price (USD)] * (1 - [Discount Pct]), 0.01) AS [Sales Amount (USD)],
    ApplyMap('MAP_ProductCost', %ProductKey, 0)                         AS [_UnitCostResolved];  // FIX F1: was [Unit Cost (USD)]
LOAD
    OrderLineID                                             AS %OrderLineKey,
    OrderID                                                 AS [Order ID],
    CustomerID                                               AS %CustomerKey,
    ProductID                                                AS %ProductKey,
    Date(Date#(OrderDateRaw,'DD/MM/YYYY'),'$(vD.Format)')     AS [Order Date],
    Date(Date#(ShipDateRaw,'DD/MM/YYYY'),'$(vD.Format)')      AS [Ship Date],
    Quantity                                                 AS [Quantity],
    Floor(UnitPriceRaw*100)/100                                AS [Unit Price (USD)],
    DiscountPct                                                AS [Discount Pct],
    SalesChannel                                               AS [Sales Channel],
    SalesRep                                                   AS [Sales Rep],
    1                                                          AS #OrderLineCounter,
    Now()                                                      AS _LoadTime,
    'Demo Generator'                                           AS _Source
RESIDENT TMP_OrderLines;

DROP TABLE TMP_OrderLines;

// FIX F4: MAP_ProductCost is deliberately NOT dropped. A mapping table
// lives outside the data model, so DROP TABLE cannot find it and ABORTS
// the reload ("Request Aborted"). Qlik discards mapping tables by itself
// at the end of the script — verified on this engine: an identical
// script with the DROP fails, and without it the model contains only the
// real tables. Do not "fix" this by adding the DROP back.

// FIX F1: remove the working lookup field before anything stores or
// reads FACT_Sales. This is the line that actually prevents the $Syn
// table — it must stay above the STORE at the end of this tab.
DROP FIELD [_UnitCostResolved] FROM FACT_Sales;

TAG FIELD [Order ID] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Quantity] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Unit Price (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Gross Sales (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Discount Amount (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Sales Amount (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Cost Amount (USD)] WITH '$measure';
TAG FIELD [Sales Channel] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Sales Rep] WITH '$dimension';

// Dimension/fact key sanity check on the fact's own row key
TMP_FactKeyCheck:
LOAD
    Count(%OrderLineKey)          AS RowCount,
    Count(DISTINCT %OrderLineKey) AS DistinctCount
RESIDENT FACT_Sales;

LET vL.FactCount    = Peek('RowCount', 0, 'TMP_FactKeyCheck');
LET vL.FactDistinct = Peek('DistinctCount', 0, 'TMP_FactKeyCheck');
IF $(vL.FactCount) <> $(vL.FactDistinct) THEN
    TRACE >>> WARNING: FACT_Sales %OrderLineKey is not unique ($(vL.FactCount) rows vs $(vL.FactDistinct) distinct);
ELSE
    TRACE >>> FACT_Sales %OrderLineKey uniqueness OK ($(vL.FactDistinct) order lines);
END IF
DROP TABLE TMP_FactKeyCheck;


// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// DIM_Date (master calendar)
// Grain: one row per calendar date
// Source: derived from FACT_Sales' min/max [Order Date] (built while
//         FACT_Sales is still resident, below)
// Notes: associates to FACT_Sales purely via the shared field name
//        [Order Date] — no synthetic key, since exactly one other
//        table (FACT_Sales) carries that field name. [Ship Date] is
//        the fact's only other date and is deliberately left
//        unlinked (one canonical date per fact); if ship-date
//        analysis becomes a requirement, add a proper canonical-date
//        pattern (aliased calendar or link table) rather than a
//        second direct association to DIM_Date.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
TMP_DateRange:
LOAD Min([Order Date]) AS MinDate, Max([Order Date]) AS MaxDate
RESIDENT FACT_Sales;

// Num() around Peek() is defensive: it guarantees the variables hold
// date serials, so the arithmetic below cannot be broken by a dual
// value expanding as a 'YYYY-MM-DD' string and being read as
// subtraction. The *Label variables carry the readable form for TRACE.
LET vD.MinDate      = Num(Peek('MinDate', 0, 'TMP_DateRange'));
LET vD.MaxDate      = Num(Peek('MaxDate', 0, 'TMP_DateRange'));
LET vD.MinDateLabel = Date($(vD.MinDate), '$(vD.Format)');
LET vD.MaxDateLabel = Date($(vD.MaxDate), '$(vD.Format)');
DROP TABLE TMP_DateRange;

TMP_DateSeed:
LOAD
    Date($(vD.MinDate) + IterNo() - 1, '$(vD.Format)') AS [Order Date]
AUTOGENERATE 1
WHILE $(vD.MinDate) + IterNo() - 1 <= $(vD.MaxDate);

DIM_Date:
LOAD
    [Order Date],
    Year([Order Date])                                            AS [Calendar Year],
    Num(Month([Order Date]))                                      AS [Month Number],
    // FIX: Date(x,'MMM') keeps the full date serial as the dual's numeric
    // side, so [Month Name] had 730 distinct values instead of 12 and was
    // unusable as a dimension. Month() returns a proper 1-12 dual, which
    // also sorts Jan..Dec correctly with no sort expression.
    Month([Order Date])                                           AS [Month Name],
    Date(MonthStart([Order Date]),'MMM-YYYY')                     AS [Month Year],
    'Q' & Ceil(Month([Order Date])/3)                              AS [Quarter Label],
    'Q' & Ceil(Month([Order Date])/3) & '-' & Year([Order Date])   AS [Quarter Year],
    Week([Order Date])                                            AS [Week Number],
    WeekYear([Order Date])                                        AS [Week Year],
    Day([Order Date])                                             AS [Day of Month],
    // FIX: same defect as [Month Name] -- Date(x,'ddd') carried the date
    // serial, giving 730 distinct values instead of 7. WeekDay() is a proper
    // 0-6 dual that sorts Mon..Sun.
    WeekDay([Order Date])                                         AS [Day Name],
    If(WeekDay([Order Date]) >= 5, 1, 0)                          AS _IsWeekend,
    If(Year([Order Date]) = Year($(vL.Today)), 1, 0)              AS _IsCurrentYear,
    If(Year([Order Date]) = Year($(vL.Today))
       and Month([Order Date]) = Month($(vL.Today)), 1, 0)        AS _IsCurrentMonth
RESIDENT TMP_DateSeed;

DROP TABLE TMP_DateSeed;

TAG FIELD [Calendar Year] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Month Name] WITH '$dimension';
TAG FIELD [Quarter Label] WITH '$dimension';

// Calendar coverage / uniqueness check
TMP_DateKeyCheck:
LOAD
    Count([Order Date])          AS RowCount,
    Count(DISTINCT [Order Date]) AS DistinctCount
RESIDENT DIM_Date;

LET vL.DateCount    = Peek('RowCount', 0, 'TMP_DateKeyCheck');
LET vL.DateDistinct = Peek('DistinctCount', 0, 'TMP_DateKeyCheck');
IF $(vL.DateCount) <> $(vL.DateDistinct) THEN
    TRACE >>> WARNING: DIM_Date [Order Date] is not unique ($(vL.DateCount) rows vs $(vL.DateDistinct) distinct);
ELSE
    TRACE >>> DIM_Date covers $(vL.DateDistinct) calendar days ($(vD.MinDateLabel) to $(vD.MaxDateLabel));
END IF
DROP TABLE TMP_DateKeyCheck;

CALL storeAndDrop('DIM_Date', '$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Date.qvd');
CALL storeAndDrop('FACT_Sales', '$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_FACT_Sales.qvd');


///$tab Data Model
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Data Model
   Purpose: thin, optimised loads only — no transformations, no
            aliases, no WHERE beyond single-argument WHERE EXISTS().
            This is what actually ends up in the app's data model.
   Inputs:  Transform_*.qvd     Outputs: none (in-memory tables)
   Note:    after FIX F1 these four loads produce a clean star —
            FACT_Sales shares exactly one field name with each
            dimension (%CustomerKey, %ProductKey, [Order Date]) and
            the dimensions share none with each other, so there is no
            $Syn table and no circular reference.
   ===================================================== */

FACT_Sales:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_FACT_Sales.qvd] (qvd);

DIM_Customer:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Customer.qvd] (qvd);

DIM_Product:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Product.qvd] (qvd);

DIM_Date:
LOAD * FROM [$(vP.QVD_Transform)Transform_DIM_Date.qvd] (qvd);


///$tab Exit
/* =====================================================
   TAB: Exit
   Purpose: final safety net (nothing temporary should remain in
            memory — every TMP_ table was dropped in the tab that
            created it; mapping tables are discarded by Qlik itself
            and must NOT be dropped explicitly), closing trace,
            script exit.
   Inputs:  none                Outputs: none
   ===================================================== */

TRACE >>> ------------------------------------------------------;
TRACE >>> Sales Demo (Desktop) reload complete — script version $(vL.ScriptVersion);
TRACE >>> QVD Extract path:   $(vP.QVD_Extract);
TRACE >>> QVD Transform path: $(vP.QVD_Transform);
TRACE >>> FACT_Sales: $(vL.RowsOrderLines) synthetic order lines targeted;
TRACE >>> DIM_Customer: $(vL.RowsCustomers) synthetic customers targeted;
TRACE >>> DIM_Product: $(vL.RowsProducts) synthetic products targeted;
TRACE >>> Started $(vL.ScriptStartTime), finished $(Now());
TRACE >>> ------------------------------------------------------;

EXIT SCRIPT;
